{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Code Quality Review",
  "description": "Analyzes modified source code files for potential improvements including code smells, design patterns, and best practices. Generates suggestions for improving readability, maintainability, and performance while preserving existing functionality.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "*.ts",
      "*.html",
      "*.css"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "Analyze the modified file for potential code quality improvements. Focus on:\n\n1. Code smells (long methods, duplicated logic, magic numbers, deep nesting)\n2. Design pattern opportunities (better use of Angular signals, standalone component patterns, inject() usage)\n3. Best practices (proper typing, null safety, Observable/signal hygiene, separation of concerns)\n4. Readability (naming clarity, function length, comment quality)\n5. Maintainability (single responsibility, coupling, cohesion)\n6. Performance (unnecessary re-renders, missing trackBy, unsubscribed Observables, inefficient Firestore queries)\n\nProvide concise, actionable suggestions. Do not rewrite the entire file — just highlight specific areas and recommend targeted improvements. Maintain existing functionality."
  }
}